-Aggregate optimization quality should use the geometric mean across tasks, with failed tasks contributing zero to correctness reporting and being tracked separately from the geomean of valid speedups.
+Aggregate optimization quality uses `geomean_speedup_correct`, the geometric mean of verified positive speedups only. `mean_score_with_failures` is the separate failure-inclusive quality metric; it averages every normalized task score, including zero for every non-verified attempt.
 
